reAL's built-in HRTF set (hrtf=builtin, compiled into dsound.dll) is made from the following data.
src/hrtf_kemar_data.h carries the same notice.

MIT KEMAR HRTF measurements, "compact" set: Bill Gardner and Keith Martin, MIT Media Lab, 1994
("HRTF Measurements of a KEMAR Dummy-Head Microphone", MIT Media Lab Perceptual Computing Technical
Report #280).  Provided by MIT without usage restrictions.
